{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/lunar-exalted/67711-terrestrial-lunars","id":67711,"title":"Terrestrial Lunars","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Lunar Exalted"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-02-07T21:46:27-08:00","id":67711,"title":"Terrestrial Lunars","content":"So, here's a thought from another thread asking why lunars are celestial. How would changing lunars to DB power level beings, but ones with a far larger number of lunars running about (whether because they breed like DB's or just because Luna tends to choose a lot more), impact the setting? Mechanically how would you change them (with the cavaet that I'm certainly going to wait until 3E before even trying this).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1458-newk","name":"NewK","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"360"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-07T23:44:16-08:00","id":67751,"title":"","content":"Honestly, the change to the setting depends entirely on how their exaltation works.<br /> <br /> If they can reproduce in the way DB's can, I am going to assume they are organized, much like the DB's, though probably less in an empire-esque way, more like Creation's largest, continent-spanning barbarian tribe. If your child can, like you, become a terrifying wolf-monster, you'd want to keep him around. And with their ability to make lots of children really fast, they'd probably be making huge amounts of supersoldierbabies and many, many beastmen. If you have that, a large part of the setting will start revolving around either an upcoming war, a cold war or an actual war between the DB's and this Lunar supertribe. Personally, I'd say it hurts the setting, as it would focus too much on a continent-scale war, instead of more personal heroics.<br /> <br /> If there are way more of them because Luna just picks a lot more than the other Incarnae do, the group will probably be less focused and a lot more splintered, with all sorts of smaller factions and subgroups. While this would let you do more personal things, due to the Lunars not being able to be as powerful as they were before.<br /> <br /> You can't really say much about these new lunars until you have clearly defined how powerful they really are, what abilities they keep and which are weakened. Can they still make beastmen? Are they still shapeshifters? How does a Solar Bond work?<br /> Though personally, I think that it'd be better to keep them low in number. Being a large group is kind of the DB's thing, and while a second group that works like that wouldn't be a problem, I would first like to know what they are like.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I made some Martial Arts for 3e, look at them <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/723442-survival-is-fury-the-monster-reborn-ex3\" target=\"_blank\">here</a> and <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/761356-orgiastic-fugitive-style-3e\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/632-while-my-guitar","name":"While My Guitar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar632_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"606"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T00:40:27-08:00","id":67772,"title":"","content":"Why not combine the two?<br /> <br /> Terrestrial-level Lunars can &quot;Exalt&quot; other people; note, this doesn't mean they go up to you and go &quot;BLAM, now you are Exalted!&quot; No, instead they spread it by forcing the chance of Exaltation coming up to a much greater level.<br /> <br /> So, in other words, imagine if DBs were all reduced to Breeding 0 permanently. That's the normal &quot;chance&quot; of Exaltation of Lunars in the population (probably lower, though); however, when they use their spookity JOIN US IN BEING A MONSTER powers (making someone a Beastman, making someone a Lycanthrope, reproduce the Milgram experiment, whatever), it raises a person's effective &quot;Breeding&quot; to 1 or 2.<br /> <br /> I'd pitch it as Lunars being a result of Gaia and Luna building a survival &quot;back-up&quot; into Mortals; much like DBs were originally supposed to be soldiers, Lunars were originally intended as a way to prevent the Primordials from driving humanity extinct as an offensive tactic.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I have decided, after some thought, that I don't really feel happy on these forums. I might decide to come back to post. Who knows - but right now, I'm gone.<br /> <br /> So good bye, good luck, and have a nice day.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1170-amechra","name":"amechra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1170_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2316"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T01:58:48-08:00","id":67795,"title":"","content":"Speaking of combining the two, here, <a href=\"http://forums.whitewolfarchive.com/defaultd1c6-3.html?g=posts&amp;t=82643\" target=\"_blank\">have an empire of Terrestrial Gatormen.</a>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T06:35:19-08:00","id":67865,"title":"","content":"I would make the Lunar Exaltation into a disease- something inspired by the classical stories about lycanthropy. The basic idea is that people could be infected by a Lunar Exalted, and if they survive it they transform into Lunars by themselves. The severance of the disease and the criticisms to decide one's survival would decide the whole power level of the splat- that is, if anyone could be infected by a Lunar at any time and there are high chances for survival, I'll make the Lunars a lot less powerful than if the disease could be infected under the Lunar's Aspect and that in order to survive it one must belong to the direct bloodline of the said Lunar and even than only one out of five survives.<br /> <br /> That would, of course, also effect their shape-shifting abilities. In the most extreme case in which it is easy to spread the Lunar Exaltation, their transformation abilities would greatly diminish, maybe even binding them only to their spirit form unless they seek power in the Wyld in form of Chimerism- in which you exchange your sanity for power. If the disease would be in the other extreme, than I may allow them keep their shapeshifting as is, with making Knacks and their like more expansive.<br /> <br /> Sorcery, Necromancy and Martial Arts would, again, be limited according to the chances to survive the Exaltation, but even at their highest they would be limited, with being just a little bit above Dragon Blooded- Terrestrial Sorcery (with an option to Celestial under the right education), Shadowland Necromancy and Terrestrial Martial Arts (again, could be Celestial with help)<br /> <br /> At least, those are my two cents :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-02-08T18:45:48-08:00","id":68184,"title":"","content":"I don't have much to contribute to this topic, but I thought I should note that while I haven't read their work, a user actually <a href=\"http://exalted.xi.co.nz/wiki/Haku/Faint_Moon\" target=\"_blank\">homebrewed something like this</a> as a side project back in 1e. It was designed relative to First Edition Lunars, and has never been adapted to 2e mechanics or fluff, but it's possible that there's something worth pilfering from the work. If nothing else, it's an interesting coincidence.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/104-gayo","name":"Gayo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar104_2.gif","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1948"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}